11
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,678
Your agent can build almost anything. But it still picks one

12
00:00:02,678 --> 00:00:05,355
model for everything.

21
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:12,268
A frontier model to classify a support ticket. To generate a

22
00:00:12,268 --> 00:00:17,036
barrel prop. To draft a thumbnail. Most of that spend is wasted.

31
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,790
This is ModelPick. A decision layer that picks the best value

32
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:25,581
at every node — not the cheapest, the best price-performance

33
00:00:25,581 --> 00:00:29,371
— and prices it in cost per solved task.

41
00:00:30,171 --> 00:00:34,315
Inside Claude Code, ask for a game-ready 3D asset. ModelPick

42
00:00:34,315 --> 00:00:38,459
compares Tripo, Hunyuan, and Meshy, applies the constraints,

43
00:00:38,459 --> 00:00:42,603
and returns one recommendation with the real cost. Twenty-one

44
00:00:42,603 --> 00:00:46,747
cents per usable asset.

51
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:51,124
For a launch video, it plans the whole pipeline. Script, keyframes,

52
00:00:51,124 --> 00:00:54,701
clips, voice, music. Five models, one budget, before a single

53
00:00:54,701 --> 00:00:58,278
frame renders.

61
00:01:00,547 --> 00:01:04,351
One command installs it into Codex, Cursor, DeepSeek Harness,

62
00:01:04,351 --> 00:01:08,156
or Copilot. A CLI, an MCP server, and a skill. No gateway. No

63
00:01:08,156 --> 00:01:11,960
keys stored.

71
00:01:13,547 --> 00:01:17,813
Every price has a source. Every decision is benchmarked. And

72
00:01:17,813 --> 00:01:22,080
the entire catalog is a JSON file you can change.

81
00:01:23,547 --> 00:01:27,440
ModelPick. Stop paying frontier prices for non-frontier work.

82
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:31,334
Open source. MIT. On GitHub.
